  "novel_mechanics_found": "Five hard mechanical decodes this round. (1) ACTION7 IS AN UNDO: it exactly reverses the last effective carrier move (verified twice: A7 after a W-press restored all four shifted carriers; A7 after an S-press restored them again). Round 7 misread it because the undone moves were off-view east-carrier moves. (2) ACTION5 WORKS IN L7 even though frame.available_actions=[1,2,3,4,6,7] omits it: A5 arms a KEYHOLE mode (state_key bool zvcnglshzcx flips True and a key/lock overlay renders at px rows 51-63 x2-12, plus padlock glyphs recolor the two sealed chamber pieces), and a click on the keyhole at px (7,56) [grid (0,8)] executes an IN-LEVEL RESET: all six carriers snap back to the L7 start config (5,5),(14,2),(18,3),(19,2),(20,3),(22,4) and the mode disarms. This is the L7-scoped reset round 7 hunted for -- and the L6 banked solution (index 442: action 5 then click (7,56)) used the same A5+keyhole idiom, so it is likely a standing per-level mechanic. (3) EAST RAIL NETWORK FULLY MAPPED BLIND via state_key: one shared row-2 line x16..22 plus four pure-vertical south spurs at even columns only -- col16 to y3, col18 to y4, col20 to y5, col22 to y4 (odd columns 17/19/21 have NO spurs; verified by parking carriers there and pressing S). The four east carriers are interchangeable walkers on this one network and block each other cell-wise; the elevator carrier's top rail is row-1/2 x11..14 joining the known (11,1)->(9,3)box->(8,7)/(9,7)/(10,7) line, and (10,7) is its hard east end. NO east rail reaches the east peg's cell (22,6) or any cell adjacent to it. (4) MOVEMENT GRAMMAR DECODED from the banked L6 tail: pieces travel as LEAPFROG PAIRS -- click source, click landing 2 cells away crossing one occupied cell, and the crossed piece then jumps over the lander in turn (C2,2 C2,4 C2,3 C2,5 ... in the L6 trace); carriers are mobile landing cells; the camera scrolled in L6 only while a CARGO-LOADED carrier moved (13 consecutive A4 presses right after pieces boarded). (5) ACTION6 accepts x>63 without error (probed up to x=150), but no out-of-view click produced any state change, so whether clicks are world-mapped or clamped remains UNRESOLVED. NEGATIVE RESULTS: the west screen provably has no first move (every jump shape from every visible piece/lock/socket was pair-click tested, including torch-over-parked-ferry (1,7)->(1,5), chamber pieces to (0,3)/(6,3)/(0,0)/(6,0), stacked-block self-pair); parking all four east carriers at all four spur ends simultaneously unlocks nothing; carriers and locks are never selectable; piece-click-then-arrow does not move pieces; the row-0 pixel bar is a cosmetic action odometer (paints 1 px per action, second lap in color 2) and its per-click flicker is rendering noise, not a selection signal.",
