  "narrative": "Precondition: resolved the banked plan via resolve_replay_plan (615 labels from results/outer_loop_fable5_lf52_probe_l6_20260712.json), replayed from a fresh env.reset() in 1.0s, confirmed frame_level=6, state=NOT_FINISHED, win_levels=10. Then explored L7 for 103 further actions, all state_key-diffed. In order: mapped the east network by direction-press saturation (S/E/N/W sweeps), discovering the col-16 spur and that odd columns have no spurs; discovered ACTION7=undo while re-testing it around carrier moves; parked all four east carriers on all four spur ends simultaneously (no unlock); pair-click tested every constructible west-screen jump (chamber pieces, chamber locks upward, shaft torch over parked ferry to (1,5), corridor cells) -- all dead; rode the elevator to its visible cells and click-tested it (not selectable); analyzed the banked L6 tail offline and found the single ACTION5 + click(7,56) pair, tried A5 in L7 despite available_actions omitting it, and decoded the A5-armed keyhole in-level reset (used it once mid-session to restore the clean start, and once at the end so this artifact's 718-action sequence terminates at the canonical L7 start); probed out-of-view world-coordinate clicks at the east peg (138,42) and all four of its distance-2 landings plus the surrounding rows -- accepted by the env but no state change ever resulted. Dead ends are recorded honestly: no new level was won; the L7 first move remains undiscovered. The binding open question is how the design intends the player to act on the east screen: the L6 precedent (camera follows cargo) needs a loaded carrier, but every loadable piece is sealed behind locks whose landing cells are walls, and the east peg is isolated from all rails.",
